From: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 10:39:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add EIP-197 outer inline path

Program APPE service codes 7 and 8 for the inbound PPE-to-EIP-to-PPE
path and steer service-code traffic to the EIP physical port. Add ESP
3-tuple and NAT-T 5-tuple outer flows, including source-L3-interface
validation and refcounted router-MAC bindings so rekeyed SAs can share
a hardware row without leaking its dependencies.

Allocate one source-only virtual port per inbound SA. Point it at EIP
port 7, preserve the return service code and deliver exceptions through
an RCU-protected callback. Publish the EIP API only after VP setup and
revoke it before physical-port teardown, draining outer flows and
quiescing callbacks while their hardware dependencies remain valid.

Expose the resulting outer flows and VP state through debugfs.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/commit/c4f168f22ac79625460fb5c17c0d8c1664803d03
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/169bf594df03ac4b29e0ccd3f6f87e70f0f3fb6e
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/39c0281b98922dcda04f91e30dd15bccbb0896ae
Signed-off-by: Amit Gupta <quic_amitgupt@quicinc.com>
